  "description": "Three real transactions posted end to end, and the case that pins every declared width with its FILLER intact (gates G19 and G21). It is case15's seed with account 5 present, so all three of dailytran rows 0 to 2 post: row 0 to account 7 at +504.77, row 1 to account 20 at -919.00 on the type 03 key that has to be created, row 2 to account 5 at +67.88. Every record here is pinned at its copybook width and every one of them ends in a reserved span that has to be emitted for the width to come out right: the three TRAN-RECORDs at 350 bytes each end in FILLER X(20); the three account records at 300 bytes each end in FILLER X(178) and carry A000000000 in ACCT-ADDR-ZIP with ACCT-GROUP-ID as ten spaces, which is genuinely how acctdata.txt is laid out; the three cross-reference records are 50 bytes only because the 36-byte fixture rows were widened by their declared normalisation; and the category-balance records are 50 bytes with FILLER X(22) - twenty-two zeros on the two the fixture supplied and twenty-two spaces on the one INITIALIZE created. Each posted transaction also carries two 26-byte timestamps: TRAN-ORIG-TS copied from the daily record and TRAN-PROC-TS composed by Z-GET-DB2-FORMAT-TIMESTAMP, whose separators are hyphens at positions 5, 8 AND 11 - the date and the time are joined by a hyphen, not a space, unlike the ORIG-TS beside it - then dots at 14, 17 and 20 and the literal 0000 in the last four bytes. RETURN-CODE is 0 and both count lines read 000000003 and 000000000. The created category-balance record carries twenty-two ZEROS in its FILLER for the reason case15 spells out: record 0's READ succeeded first and left tcatbal row 6 in the area, and INITIALIZE at :504 does not touch FILLER.",
